## 1. Station event → EH telemetry ingest

Each station event is published to Event Hubs (smalt: `event_hubs/listener.ex:3`,
AMQP 5673; consumer groups `event_hubs.ex:847`). The browser console reaches the
emulator only through `smaltFetch` (`lib/smalt.ts`) — `assertLocalUrl` keeps it
air-gapped to loopback.

## 2. Red-Andon → SB containment workflow queue

A red Andon signal is a refusal face: `Smalt.Powl2.Andon.format_andon/4`
(`lib/smalt/powl2/andon.ex`) mints the typed receipt, and the containment workflow
rides SB station queues (`lib/smalt/powl2/sb_rules.ex`, DLQ `:powl8_sb_rules_dlq`;
AMQP 5672 `amqp_broker.ex:35`). Gate `020_red_andon_containment` refuses any red
signal without a linked containment.

## 3. Batch seal → OCEL event log

Per batch, events seal into an OCEL 2.0 log: smalt's
`Smalt.Telemetry.OcelNdjson` (`lib/smalt/telemetry/ocel_ndjson.ex`) appends one
complete OCEL 2.0 document per line and assembles batch documents fail-closed;
unrdf's `@unrdf/otel` OCEL export (`packages/otel/src/ocel/index.mjs`) is the
browser-side complement, converting OTel spans to the same event-log shape.

## 4. Browser-side SHACL

Validate station/work-order graphs in the console with the rendered
`shacl-manufacturing-shapes.ttl` (rdf-validate-shacl via `@unrdf/core`) before
admitting a batch — a graph violating any refusal law above never reaches ingest.
